From c7e59df8664689565358c27eb63f19575db21e2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Linda Etienne <lindae24@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:56:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add Excel Functions Challenge goal; idle-based passcode;
 HIDDEN_VIEWS; rest-day banner

Study gains a fourth goal tab for the Full Stack Modeller Functions Challenge
Series: a 6x8 level grid over XLOOKUP, XMATCH, SORT & SORTBY, FILTER, UNIQUE and
INDEX, a new su7 "Excel Functions" subject migrated into existing state so the
timer can log against it, and rows in the Today and ON TRACK cards. FSM_WEEKS is
a light placeholder plan with a PAUSE block Oct 26 - Nov 15 for the PMP final
push; the weekly hour targets are an assumption to be confirmed, not a decision.

Three usability fixes alongside it:

- The shell passcode relocked on every tab change, making Practice -> Muse ->
  Streaks a gauntlet. One unlock now covers all three and lapses after 15 min
  idle. The deadline is held in a ref so ordinary clicks never re-render the
  shell; an interval re-renders only when the unlock has genuinely expired.
- HIDDEN_VIEWS lets Health tabs be hidden without deleting them or their data.
  Empty by default. Deliberate stand-in for a Settings toggle, deferred past
  Nov 14.
- A rest day reads as the plan followed rather than as an absence.

Additive only: no schema change, nothing removed or renamed. Verified by parsing
the transpiled JSX with esbuild; NOT verified in a browser, because the CDNs this
page loads React, Babel and supabase-js from are unreachable from the build
environment. Needs a runtime check before merge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
